> : : 	1. I know you can convert altars -- how??
> : Sacrifice on 'em.
> 
> You don't mean #offer, do you?  That just causes the gods to
> battle and seems to almost always end up badly for me and my god.

#offer is the way to do it allright.
It causes conflict between the gods, but you should keep doing it. If
it says "Unluckily, ...." then you just lost a point of luck and the altar
didn't get converted. If it says "The newly consecrated ...." then you just
gained _2_ points of luck and the altar is now of your alignment. Keep
trying! It gets more likely that you will succeed as you gain levels.
Keep on #offering too, you get nice things!

> 
> : : 	2. I have yet to learn how to make statues do anything at all..?
> : Wield 'em and break open chests
> 
> There are sometimes magical statues which can apparently be brought
> to life?  I've had it happen accidentally, but I was wondering if
> you can animate the beasts and make friends with them.

Figurines will activate if you (a)pply them. If it's cursed, it won't be
friendly. If blessed or normal, it will be friendly. Normal statues have 
a couple of uses. Firstly, like Nubian says, wield them to smash open
chests or to kill nymphs that have just stolen everything you were carrying.
Secondly, smash the statue with a pick-axe to get a chance of creating
a spellbook. Statues that you find _sometimes_ have a spellbook inside.
Statues that you create with a cockatrice corpse don't, but if you polymorph
the statues then they become like the ones that you didn't create.

> 
> : : 	3. How do you convert a unicorn horn?
> : Uh that is a hard one
> 
> Yeah, I've done it before using nethack 2.3 a number of years ago,
> but I don't remember how anymore.  Getting back into the swing of things
> and enjoying the new thingies in 3.0.

Huh? A unicorn horn is just that. You can bless/curse/normalise a horn
with the usual holy/unholy water tricks, but a unicorn horn in itself 
has no alignment. #dip it in a potion of sickness (and a couple of others)
to create water out of a useless potion, or (a)pply it to cure blindness,
hallucination, confusion etc.

> 
> : : 	4. What gives the teleport control intrinsic?
> : Tengu
> 
> Hmmm, I thought so.  I thought I ate one, though...  Maybe not.

It's random - sometimes you get it, sometimes you don't, just like any 
of the monsters. (is telepathy from a floating eye an exception?) Try
eating things like gelatinous cubes, there are about 4 different ones you
can get. The first one you eat though, you might get none of them.
The teleport control intrinsic is very hard to get though. I have never
eaten a tengu and succeeded first time. If you don't already have intrinsic
teleport then the first time you eat one that is what you get. 
("You feel jumpy") The second time you have the chance of control, but
it's a small chance. ("You feel controlled")
